### Darb Portal — sample webhook requests
### Usable with the VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client.
### The email payload here carries no attachment bytes; the full generated payloads with
### real fixture bytes live in fixtures/payloads/ and are fired by scripts/send-sample-webhooks.sh.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. WhatsApp — exact match. Every signal agrees → AUTO_MATCHED to transaction 1.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTUxMjM0NTY3AA==",
          "from": "966551234567",
          "timestamp": "1749899520",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4471", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "a3f1c9" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 2. The same message again — idempotency. Expect disposition DUPLICATE, no new document.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTUxMjM0NTY3AA==",
          "from": "966551234567",
          "timestamp": "1749899520",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4471", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "a3f1c9" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 3. WhatsApp — ambiguous. Two Tamimi transactions, same amount, same day → NEEDS_REVIEW.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTUxMjM0NTY4AA==",
          "from": "966551234567",
          "timestamp": "1750162200",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4472", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "b7d2e1" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 4. WhatsApp — scoping. A Nujood driver sends a receipt that matches a *Rawabi* charge
### exactly; sender scoping must still refuse it. Expect UNMATCHED / NO_PLAUSIBLE_CANDIDATE.
### (This carried media_4471 — the same bytes as request 1 — so it returned DUPLICATE and
### demonstrated nothing about the rule it names.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTYxMTEyMjMzAA==",
          "from": "966561112233",
          "timestamp": "1749899520",
          "type": "image",
          "image": { "id": "media_4477", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "b7d2e4" }
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 5. WhatsApp — malformed. type says image but no image object → 400 with field-level issues.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [{
    "changes": [{
      "value": {
        "messages": [{
          "id": "wamid.BROKEN",
          "from": "966551234567",
          "timestamp": "1749899520",
          "type": "image"
        }]
      }
    }]
  }]
}

### 6. Email — malformed. Bad address, no attachments → 400.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "",
  "from": "not-an-email",
  "to": "receipts@darb.example.com",
  "receivedAt": "nope",
  "attachments": []
}

### 7. WhatsApp — the orphan. A good receipt for a charge that has not posted yet.
### Lands UNMATCHED (not FAILED), which is what leaves it eligible for the re-match sweep
### in request 8. Run this one before that one.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entry": [
    {
      "changes": [
        {
          "value": {
            "messages": [
              {
                "id": "wamid.HBgMOTY2NTUxMjM0NTcwAA==",
                "from": "966551234567",
                "timestamp": "1750338720",
                "type": "image",
                "image": { "id": "media_4474", "mime_type": "image/jpeg", "sha256": "d4e5f6" }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### 8. Transactions — the re-match trigger. Run request 7 first.
### The response reports which documents this new charge rescued:
###   {"created":[...],"rematch":{"scanned":N,"changed":1,"documents":[{"from":"UNMATCHED","to":"MATCHED"}]}}
### The Idempotency-Key is REQUIRED — this endpoint creates financial records, and the
### sweep makes a client-side timeout likely enough that a blind retry would double them.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: requests-http-late-arrival-001

{
  "transactions": [
    {
      "clientId": 1,
      "cardLast4": "4412",
      "driverPhone": "966551234567",
      "merchantName": "KUDU REST 118 RUH",
      "amount": 3300,
      "currency": "SAR",
      "transactionAt": "2025-06-19T13:12:00Z"
    }
  ]
}

### 9. Transactions — malformed. Returns 400 with one issue per bad field.
### The header is supplied so the response shows field-level validation rather than the
### missing-header refusal.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: requests-http-malformed-001

{
  "transactions": [
    { "clientId": 1, "cardLast4": "44", "merchantName": "", "amount": -5, "transactionAt": "nope" }
  ]
}

### 10. Health checks
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/email

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/whatsapp?hub.mode=subscribe&hub.challenge=12345
